WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:05.500
<b>This is a work of fiction. The names of the people, places, and organizations
are fictitious and in no way related to any real person or entity.</b>

00:05.350 --> 00:15.360
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

00:17.870 --> 00:25.370
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

00:18.530 --> 00:20.150
<i>Now that the sports festival is over,</i>

00:20.150 --> 00:22.900
<i>I actually have time 
to admire the cherry blossoms.</i>

00:22.900 --> 00:24.210
<i>The seasons have changed,</i>

00:24.210 --> 00:26.930
<i>and springtime has come again 
to Hino-Minami High,</i>

00:26.930 --> 00:28.880
<i>where Koshitan and the others go to school.</i>

00:29.460 --> 00:33.060
<i>Remember when I said this series wasn't 
stuck in the Sazae-san space-time dimension?</i>

00:33.060 --> 00:34.380
<i>Well, I lied!</i>

00:34.380 --> 00:37.640
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

00:34.380 --> 00:37.640
<i>Might be about time to enjoy some cherry-
blossom viewing in front of the clubhouse.</i>

00:38.660 --> 00:40.080
Good work, everyone.

00:49.520 --> 00:51.000
What's wrong, Shikanoko?!

00:51.000 --> 00:52.550
Oh, Koshitan.

00:52.550 --> 00:55.210
Why are you crying? Did you get hurt?

00:55.210 --> 00:58.780
Or are you hungry? 
We have plenty of deer crackers.

00:55.450 --> 00:58.780
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

01:00.400 --> 01:04.540
I'm not even sad, but I just can't 
stop crying for some reason.

01:07.640 --> 01:08.630
That's weird, right?

01:09.070 --> 01:11.340
Maybe it's because it's spring.

01:11.340 --> 01:14.090
Shikanoko... You...

01:15.590 --> 01:17.970
You probably have allergies.

02:51.020 --> 02:56.030
<b>Blame It on the Spring</b>

02:56.030 --> 02:57.780
Nah, nah, nah, nah.

02:57.780 --> 03:00.630
What are you even talking about, Koshitan?

03:00.630 --> 03:01.780
Did you happen to forget?

03:02.620 --> 03:03.910
I am a deer!

03:04.200 --> 03:05.660
I am Nokotan the deer!

03:06.050 --> 03:08.500
Allergies only affect you humans!

03:08.500 --> 03:10.540
There's no way they'd affect a deer like me!

03:12.700 --> 03:15.790
The hell is that symptom?! 
Is that actually an allergy symptom?

03:16.780 --> 03:19.170
It itches! Everything itches!

03:39.170 --> 03:42.150
I just can't stop crying. But why?

03:42.150 --> 03:44.420
I just told you. You have allergies.

03:44.420 --> 03:47.180
Objection! It's absolutely not allergies!

03:47.180 --> 03:50.100
Allergies could never bring a wild deer down!

03:50.100 --> 03:52.540
Oh? So what <i>do</i> you think is causing this?

03:52.800 --> 03:54.250
I think I have a cold!

03:55.350 --> 03:58.480
Stop being so damn stubborn! 
Those aren't cold symptoms.

03:58.480 --> 04:02.680
Also, what's with people who get allergies 
hating to ever admit they have allergies?

04:02.680 --> 04:04.840
<i>Just Allergy Things, number one:</i>

04:04.840 --> 04:07.160
<i>When people with allergies 
absolutely deny having them.</i>

04:08.280 --> 04:09.790
I wonder what that's all about.

04:09.790 --> 04:11.680
How in the world would I know?

04:11.680 --> 04:13.040
So cute...

04:13.040 --> 04:16.590
But lucky me! I can't believe I've 
happened upon this bizarre situation!

04:16.590 --> 04:19.310
I'll use this opening to disband the Deer Club—

04:22.770 --> 04:25.660
It itches! It itches! It itches!

04:39.000 --> 04:39.960
Okay! Well!

04:39.960 --> 04:43.070
Do you not have allergies, then, Koshitan?!

04:43.070 --> 04:44.850
Hm? Me?

04:44.850 --> 04:49.680
I haven't once suffered from allergies in my 
seventeen years on Earth, and I never will!

04:49.680 --> 04:51.930
<i>Just Allergy Things, number two:</i>

04:51.930 --> 04:55.590
<i>People who are oddly confident 
that they will never have them.</i>

04:56.680 --> 04:58.210
No fair, Koshitan!

04:58.210 --> 04:59.830
You're just some dumb human!

04:59.830 --> 05:02.460
Pfft, say whatever you want.

05:02.460 --> 05:03.830
You're just some former delinquent!

05:03.830 --> 05:05.610
And you like girly things, too!

05:05.610 --> 05:07.490
What's that got to do with anything?

05:07.490 --> 05:10.690
I can't go on with some human 
who doesn't understand this pain!

05:10.690 --> 05:13.080
We're disbanding the Deer Club as of today!

05:13.080 --> 05:14.310
Over something this trivial?!

05:14.310 --> 05:16.120
<i>Their paths have diverged.</i>

05:16.450 --> 05:17.780
The Deer Club is disbanding?!

05:17.780 --> 05:20.540
Yes! Finally my ambition is...

05:23.010 --> 05:26.860
Ugh! Now's not the time for that!

05:26.860 --> 05:28.880
<i>Just Allergy Things, number three:</i>

05:28.880 --> 05:32.640
<i>When people lose out on golden opportunities 
because they can't think straight.</i>

05:32.640 --> 05:35.410
I-I-I can't believe it's gotten this bad!

05:35.410 --> 05:38.320
After being villainized as an enemy 
of humanity since time immemorial,

05:38.320 --> 05:40.720
cedar pollen is finally taking its revenge!

05:40.720 --> 05:42.300
Do you have allergies, too, Kinu?

05:42.300 --> 05:43.400
<i>She does not.</i>

05:43.400 --> 05:45.400
<b>Student Council</b>

05:46.360 --> 05:48.250
Kinu, do you have any tissues?

05:49.410 --> 05:51.830
Oh, sorry. I only have this handkerchief.

05:51.830 --> 05:53.240
Want to use it?

05:53.240 --> 05:54.800
Um, Vice President,

05:54.800 --> 05:57.880
why don't we go back to the student 
council office so you can blow your nose?

06:00.850 --> 06:03.510
At least wash all that floof off of you.

06:03.510 --> 06:05.040
I'll go get you a towel.

06:09.880 --> 06:11.800
Ah, that feels so nice!

06:13.350 --> 06:16.430
But it still feels itchy deep in my antlers.

06:16.720 --> 06:18.610
Did you finish washing up?

06:19.980 --> 06:22.490
Ah, I feel alive again.

06:22.490 --> 06:24.440
What the hell am I witnessing 
right now? Yikes!

06:31.120 --> 06:33.330
Ah, all better.

06:33.330 --> 06:35.310
Here I come again.

06:37.290 --> 06:38.750
We have pollination!

06:38.750 --> 06:41.250
<i>It definitely feels like springtime is here.</i>

06:41.770 --> 06:43.590
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

06:45.460 --> 06:47.890
Dang it! It still itches!

06:47.890 --> 06:49.870
<i>Just Allergy Things, number four:</i>

06:49.870 --> 06:52.220
<i>Allergy-inspired rage that has no outlet.</i>

06:52.720 --> 06:55.660
Come to think of it, they make 
glasses for people with allergies.

06:55.660 --> 06:57.940
They're designed to keep 
pollen out of the eyes.

06:57.940 --> 06:58.990
That's what I need!

07:00.180 --> 07:03.360
Ta-dah! I borrowed some goggles 
from the swim team!

07:03.620 --> 07:04.570
Ooh.

07:04.570 --> 07:07.490
Yay! I don't itch anymore! Now I win!

07:07.490 --> 07:09.650
You ain't got nothin' on me, allergies!

07:16.140 --> 07:18.400
My antlers are itching again.

07:18.400 --> 07:19.870
Wait, what the hell was that?!

07:19.870 --> 07:21.750
Did... Did your antlers just sneeze?!

07:22.630 --> 07:24.000
Here, have some tissues.

07:24.290 --> 07:27.480
The next time you feel a sneeze coming on, 
blow your antlers with those.

07:27.480 --> 07:29.030
I want fancy tissues like Antler Celeb.

07:29.030 --> 07:30.600
Quit being picky!

07:31.840 --> 07:33.260
Hey, are you okay?

07:33.730 --> 07:36.510
My nose is stuffed up, 
so my voice is all nasally.

07:36.510 --> 07:38.770
You sound super weird!

07:39.780 --> 07:44.640
Oh, why do these horrible things 
just keep happening to me?

07:44.640 --> 07:47.900
Why are you trying to act like a tragic 
heroine with snot coming out of your nose?

07:47.900 --> 07:50.820
Living in a world like this 
is too much! I'm done!

07:50.820 --> 07:52.530
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

07:51.330 --> 07:52.530
I'm done!

07:52.530 --> 07:53.590
I'm done!

07:54.030 --> 07:55.040
I'm done!

07:54.030 --> 07:55.530
<b>Hino Zoo</b>

07:55.530 --> 07:56.600
I'm done!

07:56.950 --> 07:58.890
I'm done!

08:07.010 --> 08:10.850
Everyone... Are you here to cheer me up?

08:10.850 --> 08:12.280
Even you, Tsunoda-san?

08:13.300 --> 08:15.680
And they're here again...

08:15.680 --> 08:18.440
Thanks... I won't let this get me down!

08:18.440 --> 08:21.060
I know! I just had a great idea!

08:21.060 --> 08:23.480
Let's burn down the cedar trees!

08:23.480 --> 08:25.440
Could you not say something so ominous?

08:25.440 --> 08:28.360
Not to mention, burning down the 
cedar trees in the neighborhood

08:28.360 --> 08:29.510
isn't gonna fix your allergies—

08:29.510 --> 08:31.190
Koshitan, did you forget?

08:32.070 --> 08:35.950
My antlers have a dynamite version, too.

08:40.960 --> 08:43.990
And I've shed a lot of antlers.

08:43.990 --> 08:45.350
Don't tell me you...

08:45.350 --> 08:49.060
With these, I'm going to blow up 
every last cedar grove in Japan!

08:49.060 --> 08:52.010
Could you not store explosives 
in the clubhouse?

08:52.010 --> 08:55.910
I will return it all to nothing, so that 
a new world can rise from the ashes!

08:55.910 --> 08:58.260
What's with the final boss spiel?

08:58.260 --> 08:59.760
I want in on that plan!

08:59.760 --> 09:01.140
Nekoyamada-san?!

09:02.270 --> 09:04.410
Ah, Comrade Shikayamada.

09:04.410 --> 09:05.640
It's Nekoyamada!

09:07.180 --> 09:09.970
What's one thing our world 
would be better off without?

09:09.970 --> 09:12.760
Let me tell you... Cedars!

09:12.760 --> 09:13.900
Precisely!

09:13.900 --> 09:15.340
Say no to pollen!

09:15.340 --> 09:16.560
No to pollen!

09:16.560 --> 09:17.790
Say no to pollen!

09:17.790 --> 09:19.090
No to pollen!

09:19.090 --> 09:20.270
Say no to pollen!

09:20.270 --> 09:21.740
No to pollen!

09:23.750 --> 09:27.530
Now, hold on a sec. There's probably 
something I should mention first.

09:27.530 --> 09:29.790
Something you should mention?

09:29.790 --> 09:33.800
<b>Hino Veterinary Hospital for Doggies and Kitties</b>

09:33.800 --> 09:36.800
No! I don't like hospitals!

09:37.210 --> 09:39.410
Now, now. Just stay still for me.

09:39.410 --> 09:42.830
Why am I here, too?! I'm not a cat!

09:42.830 --> 09:44.940
Now, now. Just stay still for me.

09:44.940 --> 09:48.020
Don't hate me. This is part 
of my job as your owner.

09:48.020 --> 09:50.270
Here I come again!

09:52.730 --> 09:55.650
Koshi-san, you can head 
into the exam room next.

09:55.650 --> 09:56.530
Huh?!

09:56.750 --> 09:58.780
<i>Just Allergy Things, number five:</i>

09:58.780 --> 10:03.930
<i>When someone who swears they'll never 
suffer from allergies finally gets them.</i>

10:04.540 --> 10:08.040
<b>Izu Peninsula
Hachijo-jima</b>

10:08.040 --> 10:11.540
<b>Hachijo-jima
Reeves's muntjacs</b>

10:11.540 --> 10:13.550
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

10:13.550 --> 10:17.420
Shikanoko hasn't been coming 
to the Deer Club lately.

10:17.420 --> 10:20.430
Damn it. Where's she slacking off at?

10:20.430 --> 10:26.930
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

10:20.760 --> 10:23.590
So it's been a week since she 
was last at the clubhouse...

10:23.590 --> 10:25.810
That's actually pretty long.

10:27.380 --> 10:31.030
We can't do Deer Club activities 
without our deer!

10:31.030 --> 10:33.530
What could she possibly be up to, and where?

10:33.530 --> 10:37.520
She's been coming to school, so it's just her 
after-school whereabouts that are unknown.

10:37.520 --> 10:41.810
Wait! Did she quit the Deer Club 
and join some other club?!

10:41.810 --> 10:46.950
Oh, no... This castle I've made for myself, 
not to mention the Deer Club, is in peril!

10:46.950 --> 10:49.840
A club with no deer cannot stand!

10:50.160 --> 10:53.710
We can't just sit here! We're going 
to look for Shikanoko, you two!

10:53.710 --> 10:55.590
Aw...

10:56.650 --> 10:57.710
<i>Damn it.</i>

10:57.710 --> 11:01.350
<i>Somehow, I ended up having 
to look for her all by myself.</i>

11:03.470 --> 11:05.470
<b>Flower Arrangement Club</b>

11:04.040 --> 11:05.470
Yay!

11:05.470 --> 11:07.470
<b>Flower Arrangement Club</b>

11:06.010 --> 11:07.470
<i>The Flower Arrangement Club?</i>

11:08.570 --> 11:10.730
<i>It seems oddly lively.</i>

11:10.940 --> 11:15.710
Ahem. We have a special 
lecturer visiting us today.

11:15.710 --> 11:17.190
This is Nokotan-sensei.

11:18.480 --> 11:20.360
<i>There she is!</i>

11:21.270 --> 11:22.740
Nokotan-sensei!

11:22.740 --> 11:23.870
You're so amazing!

11:23.870 --> 11:26.450
<i>Wh-What the hell is Shikanoko doing 
in the Flower Arrangement Club?</i>

11:26.450 --> 11:28.100
<i>And what did she mean by special lecturer?</i>

11:28.100 --> 11:31.920
Now, let's have our lecturer 
perform a flower arrangement.

11:31.920 --> 11:33.880
Sensei, if you would.

11:34.380 --> 11:38.130
<i>Wha? Like she'd know anything 
about flower arrangement.</i>

11:38.440 --> 11:39.850
Very well.

11:40.970 --> 11:42.700
<i>What's this sudden atmosphere?</i>

11:43.070 --> 11:47.640
<i>Could she have some knack for it 
that I didn't know about?</i>

11:47.940 --> 11:50.390
Shikanoko Style Technique...

11:53.450 --> 11:54.270
Yeah, nope.

12:06.190 --> 12:08.470
Don't use your damn head for a flower bed!

12:08.470 --> 12:10.290
There's a thing called being too free!

12:10.290 --> 12:12.140
That's so impressive, Nokotan-sensei!

12:12.140 --> 12:14.630
Rather than flowers, she arranged her antlers!

12:14.630 --> 12:16.290
What a wonderful idea!

12:16.520 --> 12:19.170
<i>So you agree. 
It's not a flower arrangement at all.</i>

12:50.120 --> 12:52.110
I-I've never seen such technique!

12:52.110 --> 12:53.120
<i>What</i> technique?!

12:53.380 --> 12:55.810
Her flower-less arrangement 
was already impressive,

12:55.810 --> 12:58.910
but with her bold new crumb-
scattering idea on top of that...

12:58.910 --> 13:01.660
This could change the history 
of flower arrangement forever!

13:02.680 --> 13:04.630
It's a revolution in the 
flower-arrangement world!

13:04.630 --> 13:08.010
<i>Again, this isn't even 
flower arrangement anymore.</i>

13:08.750 --> 13:11.820
I knew my eye for talent didn't fail me!

13:16.520 --> 13:20.020
May a thousand antlers bloom!

13:22.680 --> 13:27.530
I still haven't forgotten how your artwork 
that day resonated with my very soul!

13:27.950 --> 13:32.910
Now, Nokotan-sensei, would you be so kind 
as to tell us the title of this piece?

13:34.470 --> 13:36.050
"Tsuno to Shika."

13:36.050 --> 13:38.920
<i>Sounds very similar to a Yonezu Kenshi 
song title from a while back.</i>

13:40.500 --> 13:42.540
It's... It's just so deep!

13:42.540 --> 13:45.630
How?! It's not deep! 
It's actually pretty damn shallow!

13:45.940 --> 13:49.330
So this uses the deer crackers 
to represent the parched earth

13:49.330 --> 13:53.580
and expresses the bond that was born 
from deer and humans living together.

13:53.580 --> 13:54.470
It's genius!

13:54.470 --> 13:57.770
This is amazing, Nokotan-sensei. I'm in awe.

13:57.770 --> 13:59.980
<i>You're </i>seriously<i> overthinking this.</i>

14:01.880 --> 14:06.280
Now, let's have Nokotan-sensei 
observe all of your works.

14:06.280 --> 14:08.130
Sensei! Please look at mine!

14:08.130 --> 14:09.180
No, mine!

14:09.180 --> 14:10.360
Mine first!

14:10.360 --> 14:13.770
Yes, yes. I'll look at all of yours 
in order, one at a time.

14:13.770 --> 14:15.680
<i>What is this, an idol handshake event?!</i>

14:17.000 --> 14:21.750
Um... I tried to express the beauty 
of springtime with this piece.

14:21.750 --> 14:27.820
It's quite lovely. But I also 
feel like it lacks impact.

14:27.820 --> 14:31.500
<i>I mean, considering what you all just saw, 
everything's gonna lack impact.</i>

14:31.500 --> 14:33.380
What do you think, Sensei?

14:34.110 --> 14:35.310
Well...

14:36.100 --> 14:38.540
Um, well, er, you know...

14:38.890 --> 14:40.480
It needs better nutrition.

14:40.480 --> 14:43.400
Are you giving advice to some college freshman 
that just started living on their own?!

14:43.690 --> 14:44.840
Oh, I see!

14:44.840 --> 14:46.650
What exactly made sense there?!

14:46.650 --> 14:49.930
All you need is a bit of wildness, 
cuteness, umami, and some antlers.

14:49.930 --> 14:51.640
And a pinch of salt.

14:51.640 --> 14:55.160
You're right! How did I not notice it before?

14:55.430 --> 14:59.080
<i>Is that necessary? No, really. Is any of 
that necessary for flower arrangement?</i>

14:59.320 --> 15:02.030
This is what you get once 
you add all those things.

15:02.030 --> 15:03.080
So graphic!

15:03.360 --> 15:05.610
<i>Where'd the "beauty of spring" aspect go?!</i>

15:05.610 --> 15:10.090
<i>Are we in a jungle?! Also, don't 
just add onto someone else's piece!</i>

15:10.090 --> 15:11.240
It's lovely!

15:11.240 --> 15:13.090
<i>Well, as long as she's happy.</i>

15:13.090 --> 15:14.940
And for the final touch...

15:20.560 --> 15:24.110
Uh, why a guitar?! And do you have an 
extra-dimensional pocket in there?!

15:46.580 --> 15:48.750
<i>Uh... What even is this performance?</i>

15:48.750 --> 15:50.870
<i>It's not even a proper song.</i>

15:53.360 --> 15:55.480
Oh god, it's moving!

15:55.480 --> 15:58.600
Wait, I've seen these things on TV before!

15:58.600 --> 16:01.230
The flowers... are alive!

16:01.230 --> 16:03.310
With the sound of music?!

16:03.310 --> 16:05.110
Talk about lame!

16:05.110 --> 16:09.030
I knew I was right about you, 
Nokotan-sensei! My eyes never lie—

16:11.590 --> 16:15.870
See? This is what you get for 
saying something so clichéd!

16:15.870 --> 16:19.550
So you're saying that with birth 
also comes death!

16:19.550 --> 16:22.100
It's the circle of life!

16:22.100 --> 16:25.880
The god of the flower arrangement world—
no, of the new world has been born!

16:25.880 --> 16:28.120
She's a shoo-in for the Nobel Prize!

16:28.120 --> 16:31.630
All of you, quit flower arrangement right now!

16:34.620 --> 16:37.760
Oh, dearie me. It's about 
time to leave school.

16:37.760 --> 16:41.850
Sensei—no, O God! 
Please continue tomorrow.

16:41.850 --> 16:43.820
I won't be coming tomorrow.

16:43.820 --> 16:46.270
What?! Then the day after tomorrow?

16:46.270 --> 16:48.340
I won't be coming to the Flower 
Arrangement Club anymore.

16:48.340 --> 16:52.030
No! But you have so much talent! So why?!

16:52.030 --> 16:53.280
The novelty's worn off!

16:53.280 --> 16:54.900
Don't go!

16:54.900 --> 16:57.440
What'll happen to the new world you've shown us?

16:57.440 --> 16:58.190
Don't care!

16:59.140 --> 17:00.840
The Flower Arrangement Club's scary.

17:02.290 --> 17:04.290
<b>The Next Day</b>

17:02.290 --> 17:04.290
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

17:12.100 --> 17:13.800
Nothing beats the Deer Club.

17:13.800 --> 17:14.920
Oh, I see.

17:15.300 --> 17:18.300
<b>
A very cute
Reeves's muntjac
from Hachijo-jima</b>

17:28.640 --> 17:31.320
A perfect day for planting some rice!

17:39.670 --> 17:41.700
Oh, Onee-chan.

17:43.310 --> 17:44.330
Anko-chan!

17:44.640 --> 17:46.210
I'm not helping you.

17:46.960 --> 17:54.960
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

17:47.770 --> 17:50.030
But Bashame hasn't said anything yet.

17:50.030 --> 17:51.130
Did I guess wrong?

17:51.130 --> 17:53.440
No, but...

17:54.960 --> 17:57.710
Come plant some rice with me, Anko-chan.

17:57.710 --> 18:00.110
No. I don't want to get dirty.

18:00.110 --> 18:03.970
But Bashame cultivated the land, 
all to plant Bashame's rice paddy today!

18:03.970 --> 18:06.250
Bashame spent seven episodes on this!

18:06.250 --> 18:09.570
It's a product of Bashame's 
blood, sweat, and tears.

18:09.570 --> 18:10.610
Seven episodes?

18:10.610 --> 18:14.520
Come on. Bashame promises you 
a completely new experience.

18:14.520 --> 18:16.310
I'm going to pass.

18:16.310 --> 18:17.920
You just won't take the bait.

18:17.920 --> 18:19.310
I'll take that as a compliment.

18:19.310 --> 18:22.720
Also, you didn't get permission from the 
school for your rice paddy, did you?

18:22.720 --> 18:24.580
Of course not!

18:24.580 --> 18:26.430
<i>This could very well be a crime.</i>

18:30.630 --> 18:34.510
Um... Who were you again?

18:34.510 --> 18:36.130
Tsu... Tsu...

18:36.130 --> 18:37.120
Tsudayama!

18:37.120 --> 18:38.020
You mean Tsucchi.

18:38.020 --> 18:40.390
Yes, exactly. Tsucchi.

18:40.390 --> 18:43.260
Tsucchi! Let's plant some rice together!

18:43.260 --> 18:45.270
Stare...

18:47.270 --> 18:50.270
Stare...

18:53.270 --> 18:59.800
Okay, now that you've agreed, 
it's time to plant some rice!

19:01.030 --> 19:02.530
Good luck out there.

19:02.530 --> 19:05.380
Ricey rice, ricey rice.

19:02.530 --> 19:07.790
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

19:05.380 --> 19:09.790
Hino City specialty Bashame Rice.

19:09.790 --> 19:13.670
Come one, come all.

19:13.670 --> 19:17.660
If you have a moment, come have a bite.

19:17.660 --> 19:22.300
Some delicious, delicious, Bashame Rice.

19:30.310 --> 19:33.370
Ooh, not bad, Tsudayama.

19:37.250 --> 19:40.030
It looks like it's time for Bashame 
to reveal her true power!

19:51.310 --> 19:53.900
Aw, now we have to start all over.

19:54.780 --> 19:59.030
But this isn't enough to keep Bashame down.

20:00.100 --> 20:04.230
Ooh, so you're still rarin' to go, Tsudayama.

20:04.230 --> 20:06.800
In that case, let's do this again.

20:13.690 --> 20:17.320
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

20:17.580 --> 20:20.570
Hey, you two. Are you 
done planting your rice?

20:21.260 --> 20:23.030
Oh, Anko-chan.

20:23.300 --> 20:25.320
We just finished.

20:26.470 --> 20:29.280
Wow, planting rice really is dirty work.

20:29.280 --> 20:31.610
I'm glad I didn't help out after all.

20:33.920 --> 20:35.210
Rice balls!

20:35.690 --> 20:36.790
Wow...

20:42.170 --> 20:43.800
Yummy!

20:43.800 --> 20:47.650
Your rice balls can easily 
get three stars, Anko-chan!

20:47.650 --> 20:50.560
Well, I'm honored. Are you 
enjoying your meal, too?

20:53.780 --> 20:56.600
You're really nice, Anko-chan.

20:56.600 --> 20:59.730
Not really. I'm just used 
to making packed lunches.

20:59.730 --> 21:03.360
Oh? So you make the
packed lunches, Anko-chan?

21:03.360 --> 21:06.540
Yeah, because my sister sucks at cooking.

21:15.190 --> 21:18.210
The rice planting's all done.

21:19.930 --> 21:23.920
What should we do next?

21:34.470 --> 21:36.420
Since you're growing rice and all...

21:37.530 --> 21:39.170
Why don't you pickle some plums?

21:40.520 --> 21:42.530
Anko-chan, that's...

21:43.240 --> 21:44.530
genius!

21:46.200 --> 21:48.900
Well, I guess we know what you're doing next.

21:49.220 --> 21:50.030
Yes!

21:50.030 --> 21:59.770
<b>Deer Club
Seeking New Club Members</b>

21:50.510 --> 21:55.640
Let's have a rice ball party in the fall with 
some Bashame Rice and Bashame Pickled Plums!

21:55.640 --> 21:56.740
Sounds good.

21:56.740 --> 22:00.950
We should get some chickens 
so we can eat some egg over rice, too.

22:00.950 --> 22:03.590
Sure. Some yakitori would be good, too.
